# ~/.ssh/config — symlinked here by install.sh. Host aliases so moving files
# between machines is `scp file brovo:` and not a 100.x address looked up by
# hand every time.
#
# There are no HostName lines below on purpose. ssh falls back to using the
# alias itself as the hostname, and Tailscale's MagicDNS resolves these names
# tailnet-wide, so the alias IS the address. That also means the names follow
# the machine: they resolve the same whether it is on this desk or behind
# someone else's NAT, and the connection is encrypted end to end with no port
# forwarded on any router.
#
# The catch is that they resolve only while tailscaled is running. If a name
# fails while `tailscale status` still lists the machine, MagicDNS is off — add
# a HostName line by hand using the address from that output.
#
# `tailscale status` is the source of truth for both the machine list and the
# addresses. They are deliberately not copied here: this repo is public, and a
# pasted table goes stale the moment a machine is added or removed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-specific hosts go in ~/.ssh/config.local, which is NOT in this repo.
#
# This Include has to stay at the very top. ssh takes the FIRST value it sees
# for any keyword and ignores every later one, so an Include placed below the
# blocks here could never override them — it would silently lose to whatever
# this file already said. At the top, the local file wins.
#
# What belongs there: anything private or true of only one machine. Hosts with
# a literal address or a non-standard port, per-device keys, work jump boxes.
# ello's `phone` entry is the example — an address, port 8022 and its own
# keyfile, none of which should be in a public repo or apply to any other
# machine.
#
# What belongs here instead: hosts every machine shares, addressed by MagicDNS
# name rather than by address.
#
# Missing is fine. ssh treats an Include whose file does not exist as a no-op,
# so a fresh machine works with no local file at all, and install.sh does not
# create one. It also never overwrites one: config.local is not in its symlink
# list, so `git pull && ./install.sh` cannot clobber your local hosts. That is
# the whole point of splitting them out.
Include ~/.ssh/config.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Host molly ello brovo kalu buffyx
    User aditya

    # Tailscale is a WireGuard tunnel, so an idle session can sit behind a NAT
    # mapping that expires without either end noticing. These turn a silent
    # hang into a clean "Broken pipe" after ~90s.
    ServerAliveInterval 30
    ServerAliveCountMax 3

    # Reuse one TCP connection for subsequent ssh/scp/rsync to the same host.
    # Matters most for rsync over many small files, where the handshake
    # otherwise dominates. install.sh creates the socket dir with mode 700;
    # ssh refuses a ControlPath in a directory others can write.
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/sockets/%r@%h:%p
    ControlPersist 10m

Host *
    IdentityFile ~/.ssh/id_ed25519
    # Offer only the key named above. Otherwise ssh offers every key the agent
    # holds and can trip a server's MaxAuthTries before reaching the right one.
    IdentitiesOnly yes
    AddKeysToAgent yes
    # macOS-only keyword: load the passphrase from the login keychain. This
    # file is on the MacOS branch; ssh on Linux would reject it as unknown.
    UseKeychain yes
